<Layout title="Editorial policy & content standards" description="How Resumv creates resume guides and fictional examples, explains sources, handles corrections, and separates writing guidance from hiring guarantees."><article class="page-wrap article"><header class="page-heading"><h1>Useful guidance. Clear limitations.</h1><p>How Resumv creates its resume templates, examples, and advice.</p></header>
<h2>Who creates this content</h2><p>Resumv publishes the material on this website. Current guides and fictional resume examples were drafted with AI assistance. We do not claim that they were written or independently reviewed by a certified resume writer, recruiter, or career counselor.</p>
<h2>What an example means</h2><p>Candidate names, employers, projects, and performance numbers in our examples are illustrative. They are not testimonials, real hiring histories, or evidence of employment results. Replace them with your own verified facts. Never add a skill, license, degree, or achievement you do not have.</p>
<h2>Sources and original work</h2><p>Guides link to public resources such as CareerOneStop for general resume-writing context. Occupational resources help readers investigate roles; they do not endorse our examples. Templates use open-source Reactive Resume rendering code under its MIT License. Read our <a class="text-link" href="/licenses/">open-source acknowledgments</a>.</p>
<h2>What the tools can and cannot do</h2><p>The editor formats your content and creates downloadable documents. The checker applies a local writing checklist and simple word matching; it is not an employer ATS score. The summary tool arranges the facts you enter into editable sentences. None of these tools guarantees interviews, job offers, or correct parsing by every application system.</p>
<h2>Content dates and updates</h2><p>Dates on pages identify content updates, not a promise of professional review. We revise examples when an error is identified or guidance needs clarification. Employer instructions and relevant licensing authorities take precedence over generic examples, especially for regulated occupations.</p>
<h2>Corrections and feedback</h2><p>Open an issue on <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/liusha-com/resumv/issues">GitHub Issues</a> with the page URL, the issue, and a supporting source if available. Avoid including private resume contents, patient or client information, or account credentials.</p>
<h2>Privacy and access</h2><p>The tools run in your browser and do not require an account or payment. Saved documents remain on your device; export backups to keep them. See the <a class="text-link" href="/privacy/">privacy page</a> for details.</p></article></Layout>
